('61201927-70e9-4003-8bf8-54fec291c631', 'number_operations', 'year_7', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A canteen order costs $3 per sandwich for 5 sandwiches, plus a one-off $2 delivery fee. Using 5 × 3 + 2, what is the total cost?', '["$25","$13","$21","$17"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Order of operations: multiply first (5 × 3 = 15), then add the fee: 15 + 2 = 17.', 'AC9M7N04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('762cb5b4-061f-4542-8604-c67994871f1a', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A file compression app reports sizes using powers of 2. Simplify 2⁴ × 2³ as a single power of 2.', '["2^7","2^12","2^1","4^7"]'::jsonb, 0, 'When multiplying powers with the same base, add the exponents: 4 + 3 = 7.', 'AC9M8N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('31ff4a66-6c6c-4a68-b1f6-a88c297e815a', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A school choir has 15 sopranos and 20 altos. Simplify the ratio of sopranos to altos.', '["15:20","3:4","4:3","5:4"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Divide both parts by their highest common factor, 5: 15÷5=3, 20÷5=4.', 'AC9M8N05', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c6440c04-73f2-4a70-bfcf-a0f450c6f12a', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A delivery drone''s altitude change is logged as −6 + (−4) × 2 across one flight, where −4 m represents each of 2 repeated dips. What is the total altitude change?', '["−20 m","−2 m","−14 m","2 m"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Order of operations: (−4) × 2 = −8 first, then −6 + (−8) = −14.', 'AC9M8N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('0c4e2323-4f8a-49a4-a2e2-3afafc8b9189', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A survey of Year 8 students found 5/8 prefer texting over calling. Written as a decimal, what proportion is that?', '["0.58","0.685","0.375","0.625"]'::jsonb, 3, '5 ÷ 8 = 0.625.', 'AC9M8N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('879ad125-b3d4-4450-b18d-47ab3570a91f', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A concrete mix uses cement and sand in the ratio 2:5. If a builder uses 8 bags of cement, how many bags of sand are needed to keep the same ratio?', '["20 bags","12.5 bags","10 bags","16 bags"]'::jsonb, 0, '8 bags of cement is 4 times the ratio unit (2 × 4 = 8), so sand is 5 × 4 = 20 bags.', 'AC9M8N05', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('ec69271d-c661-44a5-8e49-ed45317cc5ad', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'A netball club''s registration fee is $85. An early-bird deal reduces the fee by 10%. What is the early-bird registration fee?', null, null, '10% of 85 = 8.50, so 85 − 8.50 = $76.50.', 'AC9M8N04', null, null, true, '76.50', ARRAY['$76.50', '76.5', '$76.5']::text[], null, null),
('4e81916d-c4fe-48fa-8255-42e5e8bbc70b', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'A share portfolio''s growth factor is represented by 3⁴ ÷ 3². Evaluate this expression.', null, null, '3⁴ ÷ 3² = 3² = 9.', 'AC9M8N02', null, null, true, '9', null, null, null),
('bd0bad97-da7c-49ab-a6b9-440531a29543', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A wallpaper pattern repeat is scaled by a factor described as (3²)³, representing three successive enlargements of an already-squared base pattern. What is the value of this scale factor?', '["243","729","27","216"]'::jsonb, 1, '(3²)³ = 3⁶ = 729.', 'AC9M8N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('394651c6-ba6f-40e2-9fa3-3c18392d9ce3', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A quiz show contestant''s score is calculated as (−5) × 3 + 8, for 3 questions answered wrong (−5 each) plus an 8-point bonus. What is the contestant''s score?', '["9","−23","−7","23"]'::jsonb, 2, '(−5) × 3 = −15, then −15 + 8 = −7.', 'AC9M8N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('bd1fb0d0-a3c7-489c-946b-e8a4c4d74d71', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'An esports league has 45 members, and the ratio of members who compete weekly to those who compete monthly is 4:5. How many members compete weekly?', '["25","9","36","20"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The ratio has 9 total parts, so each part is 45 ÷ 9 = 5. Weekly competitors: 4 × 5 = 20.', 'AC9M8N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('62048fad-81fb-4d8b-957f-555800a1e727', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'A gym membership costs $65 per month. It rises by 20% next year. What will the new monthly cost be?', null, null, '65 × 1.2 = 78.', 'AC9M8N04', null, null, true, '78', ARRAY['$78']::text[], null, null),
('0480986a-f5c0-492e-b302-d48cecd9160f', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'Two friends invest in a business in the ratio 3:7. If the total profit is $400, how much does the friend with the smaller share receive?', null, null, 'The ratio has 10 total parts, so each part is 400 ÷ 10 = 40. Smaller share: 3 × 40 = 120.', 'AC9M8N05', null, null, true, '120', ARRAY['$120']::text[], null, null),
('fdd2a883-9c8e-40ed-9de3-7944c6bea061', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'An engineering report includes the term 4⁰ + 4⁻¹ for a signal strength formula. What is the value of this expression?', '["1 1/4","1","4","1/4"]'::jsonb, 0, '4⁰ = 1 and 4⁻¹ = 1/4, so 1 + 1/4 = 1 1/4.', 'AC9M8N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('ad606750-1eab-48c9-ac18-c29452c17941', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'An archer''s tournament rating changes by −8 points after each of 3 poor rounds, then gains back double the total points lost in one exceptional final round. What is the net change in rating?', '["−24","+24","+16","+72"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Points lost: −8 × 3 = −24. The final round gains back double the total lost: 2 × 24 = 48. Net change: −24 + 48 = +24.', 'AC9M8N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('4c4436a7-8666-4abf-82ee-e5cbb4b94f8d', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'A signwriter mixes paint in the ratio 5:2 (blue:white) for a specific shade. She has 2 L of white paint and wants to use all of it while keeping the ratio, but only has 4 L of blue paint available. How many litres of the mixture will she be short?', '["0.5 L","3 L","1 L","2 L"]'::jsonb, 2, 'To use all 2 L of white, she needs 5 L of blue (since 2 L matches one full ratio unit). She only has 4 L, so she is short by 1 L.', 'AC9M8N05', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('a0a0eb6b-e97e-4aae-bd38-e1a2fb3670e5', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'advanced', 'short_answer', 'A café''s coffee bean order costs $84 per bag. A bulk discount reduces the cost by 1/4, and then GST of 10% is added to the discounted price. What is the final cost per bag?', null, null, '84 × 3/4 = 63, then 63 × 1.1 = $69.30.', 'AC9M8N04', null, null, true, '69.30', ARRAY['$69.30', '69.3', '$69.3']::text[], null, null),
('c84af527-12ab-4549-91b1-721370d335ad', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A tap fills a tank at a steady rate, adding 3/4 of a litre every minute. How many litres does it add in 8 minutes?', '["5.5 L","7.5 L","4.5 L","6 L"]'::jsonb, 3, '3/4 × 8 = 6 L.', 'AC9M8N05', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('8315dfcb-97b2-4d87-818f-81228855352b', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A school debate team of 24 students has 25% who are Year 8 captains-in-training. How many students is that?', '["6","2","30","20"]'::jsonb, 0, '25% of 24 = 24 ÷ 4 = 6.', 'AC9M8N04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('b0aadf2c-8668-4ed0-abc4-0cce6e9801d8', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A weather app shows 0.5 of the week ahead is forecast as rainy. Written as a fraction in simplest form, what portion of the week is that?', '["5/10","1/2","1/5","2/5"]'::jsonb, 1, '0.5 = 1/2 in simplest form.', 'AC9M8N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('ee5b0095-ddcc-4a22-9582-b313cbba14a4', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A computer''s processing benchmark is expressed as 5⁶ ÷ 5⁴. What is the value of this expression as a whole number?', '["5","125","25","10"]'::jsonb, 2, '5⁶ ÷ 5⁴ = 5² = 25.', 'AC9M8N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('86b4605c-6275-47ce-b7c2-c3b66bd276fa', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'foundation', 'short_answer', 'A skate park''s temperature reading is −3°C in the early morning shade. By the time the sun hits it, the temperature is 7°C. What is the rise in temperature (7 − (−3))?', null, null, '7 − (−3) = 7 + 3 = 10.', 'AC9M8N03', null, null, true, '10', ARRAY['10°C']::text[], null, null),
('0f040bef-1c5b-4f28-a6f3-54ea4e6ff8f8', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'An arcade reduces its token price from $2.50 to $2.00 per token. What is the percentage decrease in price?', '["25%","50%","16%","20%"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Decrease = $0.50. As a percentage of the original: 0.50 ÷ 2.50 = 20%.', 'AC9M8N04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('6b760b23-608c-4d79-abc6-7eca7a186bb7', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A recipe-scaling app uses the term 3⁻¹ to represent a shrink factor. What is its value, written as a fraction?', '["1/3","−3","3","−1/3"]'::jsonb, 0, '3⁻¹ = 1/3¹ = 1/3.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('11ccf403-54bc-48d5-b587-2dd5a480c0e7', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A red blood cell has a diameter of about 0.000008 m. Write this measurement in scientific notation.', '["8 × 10⁶","8 × 10⁻⁶","0.8 × 10⁻⁵","8 × 10⁻⁵"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Move the decimal point 6 places to get a number between 1 and 10: 8 × 10⁻⁶.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('af472d4e-7cb7-4ed0-bbba-bd5b1528bf78', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A carpenter calculates a diagonal brace length related to √98. Simplify √98 to simplest surd form.', '["2√49","49√2","7√2","14√2"]'::jsonb, 2, '98 = 49 × 2, and √49 = 7, so √98 = 7√2.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('952bc3cb-23cc-40a7-9fb5-b479c33af6f3', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A computer processes 4 × 10³ operations per second across each of 2 × 10² processors. Using (4 × 10³) × (2 × 10²), how many total operations per second is that?', '["6 × 10⁵","8 × 10⁶","2 × 10¹","8 × 10⁵"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Multiply the coefficients and add the exponents: 4 × 2 = 8, and 10³ × 10² = 10⁵, giving 8 × 10⁵.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('153117b1-dbdd-4a60-a8b3-bffdf3988ed7', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'A signal decay factor is given by 2⁻³. What is the value of this expression as a fraction?', null, null, '2⁻³ = 1/2³ = 1/8.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, '1/8', null, null, null),
('1012f59f-6aed-4179-a4f9-7c37f613de19', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A student invests $400 at a simple interest rate of 5% p.a. How much interest is earned after 3 years?', '["$60","$20","$460","$40"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Interest = 400 × 0.05 × 3 = $60.', 'AC9M9N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('afdb3cc2-f6d6-458d-837d-47728471d3ae', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A garden designer needs the combined edge length represented by √12 + √27 for a triangular garden bed. Simplify this expression.', '["5√39","5√3","15√3","√39"]'::jsonb, 1, '√12 = 2√3 and √27 = 3√3, so √12 + √27 = 2√3 + 3√3 = 5√3.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('abcfd723-be4f-4aa3-bcd0-60d10e5d0d5c', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A nebula''s mass is 3.6 × 10⁸ tonnes, spread across 4 × 10² identical dust clouds. Using (3.6 × 10⁸) ÷ (4 × 10²), what is the average mass per cloud?', '["9 × 10⁻⁶","3.6 × 10⁶","9 × 10⁵","9 × 10¹⁰"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Divide the coefficients and subtract the exponents: 3.6 ÷ 4 = 0.9, and 10⁸ ÷ 10² = 10⁶, giving 0.9 × 10⁶ = 9 × 10⁵.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('0b82cbe5-534c-43b8-aaf5-e827611e74f8', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'An amount of $600 grows to $690 after 3 years of simple interest. What annual interest rate (p.a.) was applied?', '["6%","3%","15%","5%"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Total interest = 690 − 600 = $90 over 3 years, or $30 per year. Rate = 30 ÷ 600 = 5% p.a.', 'AC9M9N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('7eecb31c-d2a8-4457-9e1c-e3cba3b6edfb', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'A tiling pattern''s scale factor is calculated as √8 × √2. What is the value of this expression?', null, null, '√8 × √2 = √16 = 4.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, '4', null, null, null),
('4869d0f2-2da6-470a-8272-c611cf6d8cb1', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'A satellite orbits at an altitude of 3.5 × 10⁵ m above a mountain peak that is 8 × 10³ m high. What is the satellite''s height above sea level, in standard (not scientific) notation?', null, null, '3.5 × 10⁵ = 350,000 and 8 × 10³ = 8,000, so 350,000 + 8,000 = 358,000.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, '358,000', ARRAY['358000', '358,000 m', '358000 m']::text[], null, null),
('726ce5cd-5a18-4404-9396-4a9b38faacf8', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'A structural engineer calculates a support length as √3 × √12 ÷ √4 for a bridge model. What is the value of this expression?', '["3","6","9","1.5"]'::jsonb, 0, '√3 × √12 = √36 = 6, then 6 ÷ √4 = 6 ÷ 2 = 3.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('589592cc-26af-4129-af3d-4034b83d16e1', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'A tech company''s total annual data usage is (2.5 × 10⁶) + (5 × 10⁵) gigabytes across two data centres. Expressed in scientific notation, what is the combined total?', '["2.5 × 10⁶","3 × 10⁶","7.5 × 10¹¹","3 × 10¹¹"]'::jsonb, 1, '2.5 × 10⁶ = 2,500,000 and 5 × 10⁵ = 500,000, so the total is 3,000,000 = 3 × 10⁶.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('57ab19ad-8d02-4d30-8e9f-497ccfd9da0a', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'advanced', 'short_answer', 'A small bakery''s monthly costs of $2,400 increase by 15% due to rising supplier prices, and the bakery then cuts $120 from its marketing budget to offset part of the rise. What are the new monthly costs?', null, null, '2400 × 1.15 = 2760, then 2760 − 120 = 2640.', 'AC9M9N03', null, null, true, '2640', ARRAY['$2640', '2,640', '$2,640']::text[], null, null),
('71bae5e7-7fc0-4013-99f4-186ce57458cc', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'A charity''s donation total of $8,000 is reduced by 12% due to processing fees, and the remaining amount is split equally among 4 local shelters. How much does each shelter receive?', '["$1,920","$1,600","$1,760","$2,000"]'::jsonb, 2, '8000 × 0.88 = 7040, then 7040 ÷ 4 = $1,760.', 'AC9M9N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('4af2f0f8-487d-48ba-8ed4-7cf3a9bbc83e', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A telecom report models signal weakening by a factor of 4⁻² for every 100 km travelled. What is the value of 4⁻²?', '["−8","1/8","16","1/16"]'::jsonb, 3, '4⁻² = 1/4² = 1/16.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('bf8ade8d-1582-420b-9ad5-937a5c95f26c', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A skateboard ramp''s diagonal support is related to √48. Simplify √48 to simplest surd form.', '["4√3","2√12","16√3","8√6"]'::jsonb, 0, '48 = 16 × 3, and √16 = 4, so √48 = 4√3.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('977120e3-792b-4372-a09c-a89dd2e0f896', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A bookstore''s $50 novel is discounted by 10% for a book fair. What is the discount amount?', '["$10","$5","$45","$40"]'::jsonb, 1, '10% of $50 = $5.', 'AC9M9N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('4c5b45a5-004b-40fd-a1e9-426f109e346a', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'foundation', 'short_answer', 'A nanoparticle''s size is written as 3 × 10⁻⁵ cm in a lab report. Write this as a standard decimal number.', null, null, '3 × 10⁻⁵ = 0.00003.', 'AC9M9N02', null, null, true, '0.00003', ARRAY['.00003', '0.00003 cm']::text[], null, null),
('9a38e2f7-64df-4165-811d-e3a18110547f', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'An HVAC technician''s cooling formula includes the term √9 × 9⁰. What is the value of this expression?', '["9","1","3","81"]'::jsonb, 2, '9^(1/2) = 3 and 9⁰ = 1, so 3 × 1 = 3.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c1f58b66-869f-47b6-aa9c-ae4dd6d9220f', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'A storage box is a perfect cube with a volume of 125 cm³. What is the length of one edge of the box?', '["41.7 cm","25 cm","15 cm","5 cm"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The cube root of 125 is 5, since 5 × 5 × 5 = 125.', 'AC9M9N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c2dc659f-a50a-437c-84cc-3ea79b37367a', 'number_operations', 'year_9', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'A school''s fundraising target is $900. So far, 40% of the target has been reached. How much money has been raised so far?', null, null, '40% of 900 = 0.4 × 900 = 360.', 'AC9M9N03', null, null, true, '360', ARRAY['$360']::text[], null, null),
('e3a6b66d-82e2-459f-827b-756d2df8dd7d', 'number_operations', 'year_10', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'Simplify: x⁵ ÷ x²', '["x⁷","x³","x²·⁵","x¹⁰"]'::jsonb, 1, 'When dividing powers with the same base, subtract the exponents: 5 − 2 = 3.', 'AC9M10N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('e5f6b754-ce98-44c9-8dcc-37a981a27c8f', 'number_operations', 'year_10', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A population of 1,000 bacteria doubles every hour. How many are there after 3 hours?', '["8,000","6,000","3,000","4,000"]'::jsonb, 0, 'After 3 doublings: 1000 × 2³ = 1000 × 8 = 8,000.', 'AC9M10N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('1d4bf435-0263-4347-9a96-e71cb09fdf17', 'number_operations', 'year_10', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Simplify: (3x²y)³', '["27x⁶y³","9x⁶y³","27x⁵y³","3x⁶y³"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Cube each factor: 3³=27, (x²)³=x⁶, y³=y³, giving 27x⁶y³.', 'AC9M10N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('e1467128-5908-4719-b304-55b1729dd45b', 'number_operations', 'year_10', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'A car worth $20,000 depreciates by 15% each year. What is it worth after 2 years (to the nearest dollar)?', '["$14,450","$15,300","$17,000","$14,000"]'::jsonb, 0, 'After year 1: 20000 × 0.85 = 17,000. After year 2: 17000 × 0.85 = 14,450.', 'AC9M10N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('401acdc7-b099-4531-8a5b-865f73fd15a8', 'number_operations', 'year_7', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A school hall can be hired for $84.50 per hour. How much does it cost to hire the hall for 4.5 hours?', '["$370.25","$380.25","$390.25","$338.00"]'::jsonb, 1, '84.50 × 4.5 = $380.25.', 'AC9M7N04', null, true, true, null, null, null, null),
('a6a4c638-c283-41e4-8716-3b50777cfa24', 'number_operations', 'year_7', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A car uses 6.4 litres of fuel per 100 km. How many litres of fuel does it use to travel 337.5 km?', '["21.6 L","22.6 L","20.6 L","24.6 L"]'::jsonb, 0, '6.4 × 337.5 ÷ 100 = 21.6 L.', 'AC9M7N05', null, true, true, null, null, null, null),
('9ad3f2a4-ad1b-4b1a-a3da-5a80e8fdbc2b', 'number_operations', 'year_7', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'A phone bill of $58.30 is split equally among 5 housemates. How much does each housemate pay?', null, null, '58.30 ÷ 5 = $11.66.', 'AC9M7N04', null, true, true, '$11.66', ARRAY['11.66']::text[], null, null),
('a4f62802-3fc0-4847-8f4b-224208ec389b', 'number_operations', 'year_7', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'A school''s water tank holds 2,450 litres. Over summer it loses 0.08 of its water to evaporation. How many litres are lost to evaporation?', '["186 L","196 L","206 L","245 L"]'::jsonb, 1, '2450 × 0.08 = 196 L.', 'AC9M7N03', null, true, true, null, null, null, null),
('2b24d18f-ae3b-45d6-8266-dab6bc2fb7e2', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A caterer needs 3.75 kg of flour per cake and is making 17 cakes for a wedding. How many kilograms of flour does she need in total?', '["63.75 kg","60.75 kg","20.75 kg","58.5 kg"]'::jsonb, 0, '3.75 × 17 = 63.75 kg.', 'AC9M8N01', null, true, true, null, null, null, null),
('02b3d8cf-ab42-4e0f-8c67-e155ad2ebac2', 'number_operations', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'A school''s electricity bill was $1,248.60 last quarter and rises by 8.5% this quarter. What is the new bill amount?', null, null, '8.5% of $1,248.60 is $106.13. The new bill is $1,248.60 + $106.13 = $1,354.73.', 'AC9M8N04', null, true, true, '$1,354.73', ARRAY['1354.73', '$1354.73']::text[], null, null),
